meta {
  name: Admin Authentication
}

docs {
  # Admin User Authentication Tests
  
  Tests for admin user login, session management, and environment selection.
  
  ## Endpoints Tested
  
  - `POST /admin-users/login` — authenticate with username/password (no auth required)
  - `POST /admin-users/sessions/select-environment` — select environment (admin session required)
  - `POST /admin-users/sessions/logout` — logout (admin session required)
  - `GET /admin-users/sessions/current` — get current session info (admin session required)
  
  ## Authentication
  
  The login endpoint requires no authentication. All session endpoints require
  the `X-Admin-Session-Token` header with a valid session token obtained from login.
  
  ## Prerequisites
  
  - An admin user must exist (created via admin-users tests or setup)
  - The admin user must have at least one environment association
  - Valid domain and solution UUIDs
  
  ## Test Data
  
  Tests use Bruno variables set by previous tests:
  - `adminUserUsername` / `adminUserPassword` — credentials from user creation
  - `adminSessionToken` — session token from successful login
  - `adminUserDomainUuid` / `adminUserSolutionUuid` — scope identifiers
  - `adminUserEnvironmentId` — an environment the user has access to
}
